  "chunk": "background information about the game mechanics, objectives, or strategies are\nprovided. Theadvanced promptoffers comprehensive guidance derived from the\noriginalZork Iinstruction manual. This includes detailed information about\nmovement and navigation commands, syntax, combat mechanics, communica-\ntion with non-player characters, and general gameplay strategies. The prompt\nalso provides context about the game’s setting and objective: exploring the\nGreat Underground Empire, collecting treasures, and depositing them in the\ntrophy case. In both conditions, models are explicitly instructed not to use the\nrestartcommand and are given the option to respond with “I give up” if they\nbelieve they are irreversibly stuck. Both prompts are provided in Appendix A.\nEach model is tested under both prompts with five independent runs per\nmodel-prompt combination, resulting in a total of 40 experimental runs. Runs\nare conducted sequentially with fresh conversation contexts to prevent any",
